From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Noxwell <beebono@yahoo.com>
Date: Thu, 6 Aug 2026 18:44:55 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 219/225] arm64: dts: rg-rotate: DVFS I2C pads SDA3/SCL3 back
 to func1 (stock value)

Live stock Android has SDA3/SCL3 at func-sel 0 (func1), matching every
other real I2C pad; the func4 here was a misread of the stock overlay
and muxed the pads away from the I2C function, so the TOP-DVFS engine's
FAN53555 transactions never reached the wire (STATE_I2C parked at 4).
With func1 and the bypass cleared, the engine completes voltage-meet
transitions (intermittently - characterization pending), which it never
did before.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/sprd/ums512-rg-rotate.dts | 15 ++++++++++-----
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/sprd/ums512-rg-rotate.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/sprd/ums512-rg-rotate.dts
index d9d40c27d..c3097b8d7 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/sprd/ums512-rg-rotate.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/sprd/ums512-rg-rotate.dts
@@ -353,14 +353,19 @@ sd0_cd: sd0-cd {
     };
 
 	/*
-	 * Stock hogs SDA3/SCL3 at func4 (overlay pinctrl): routes the pads to
-	 * the TOP-DVFS engine's autonomous I2C channel to the FAN53555
-	 * (DCDC_CPU1). Ours booted at func1, one suspect for the I2C voltage
-	 * transaction never firing. Applied via cpudvfs_dev probe.
+	 * SDA3/SCL3 carry the TOP-DVFS engine's autonomous I2C channel to
+	 * the FAN53555 (DCDC_CPU1). Live stock Android has these pads at
+	 * func-sel 0 ("func1"), the same value as every other real I2C pad
+	 * (SCL0/SDA0, SCL1/SDA1, SCL6/SDA6) - see
+	 * docs/dvfs-working-regmaps/stock_pinconf_pins.txt. The earlier
+	 * func4 setting here (a misread of the stock DT overlay) routed the
+	 * pads AWAY from the I2C function, so the engine's FAN53555
+	 * transaction never reached the wire and DCDC_CPU1 parked at
+	 * STATE_I2C=4. Applied via cpudvfs_dev probe.
 	 */
 	dvfs_i2c_pin_func: dvfs-i2c-pin-func {
 		pins = "UMS512_SDA3", "UMS512_SCL3";
-		function = "func4";
+		function = "func1";
 	};
 
 	joypad_pins_func: joypad-pins-func {
